# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) for local dev. Without this set, the
# "Google calendar" section in Settings simply doesn't render — no calendar
# UI, no error (`shell/useCalendarWiring.ts`'s GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID export).
#
# The OAuth client itself is a human step (Google console): create an
# *Internal* OAuth client of type **Web application** — NOT the sweeper's
# client — and add this origin plus https://hb.twinion.net to its authorized
# JavaScript origins, requesting
# https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.readonly.
#
# The sweeper's client id cannot be reused here, despite what issue #73's
# brief says: `sweep.py` uses a *desktop-app* client (docs/sweeper.md), and
# desktop clients have no authorized JavaScript origins at all. What is
# shared is the project and consent screen, not the client. That keeps the
# intent of the brief intact — this stays an independent per-device
# credential, and the sweeper's refresh token and Tasks/Gmail scopes are
# untouched — while being something a human can actually complete.
#
# #577/#583/#584: nothing in the browser mints a Google credential with this
# id any more, and there is no popup and no redirect. Every token — silent
# re-mint, rotation, and an interactive Connect/Reconnect press alike —
# comes from the authority (`calendar/authority-token-client.ts`, ADR-0028),
# which authenticates with the device token and never reads this variable.
# What this id still gates is only the Settings section named above; whether
# that is still the right gate is #585's question.
#
# Deployed builds read the same variable from the VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID
# Actions secret (.github/workflows/deploy-client.yml); Vite substitutes it
# at build time, so it is baked into the bundle, as an OAuth client id is
# meant to be.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# The authority's origin. LEAVE THIS UNSET — it is an override, not a
# setting, and every checked-in configuration omits it.
#
# The API is same-origin with the shell by decision (ADR-0006/0008:
# `connect-src 'self'`, no CORS anywhere), so the correct value is always
# the bundle's own origin, and `src/worker/core.worker.ts` reads that from
# `self.location.origin` at runtime rather than baking it in. In production
# a Worker route puts `hb.twinion.net/api/*` on the authority worker
# (`server/worker/wrangler.toml`); under `vite dev` the dev-server proxy in
# `vite.config.ts` forwards `/api` to `wrangler dev` on 127.0.0.1:8787.
#
# Set it only to point a bundle at an authority that is deliberately NOT its
# own origin — a staging Durable Object, a second workspace. Doing so is a
# cross-origin request the authority will not answer without a CORS lane
# that does not exist, so it also needs a proxy in front of it.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=
